@startuml
title Workstation, Skills, And Shared Host Substrate

actor "User" as User
participant "Workstation CLI / UI" as UI
participant "Workstation Session Driver" as Session
participant "Task Contract" as Task
participant "Direct Composition" as Compose
participant "Workstation Capability Server" as Capability
participant "Shared Host Interaction Substrate" as Substrate
participant "Governed Skill Invocation" as Invoke
participant "Skill Runtime\n(python/bash/ansible/wasm)" as SkillRuntime
participant "Optional Controller Planning Bridge" as ControllerBridge

User -> UI: prompt
UI -> Session: send prompt
Session -> Task: normalize boundary-complete contract
Session -> Compose: attempt direct skill composition

alt direct worker plan exists
  Compose --> Session: skill title + invocation payload
  Session -> Capability: ws.skill.invoke(...)
  Capability -> Substrate: attachments + delegation + receipts
  Substrate -> Invoke: governed skill invocation
  Invoke -> SkillRuntime: execute selected worker
  SkillRuntime --> Invoke: result
  Invoke --> Substrate: result + traces
  Substrate --> Capability: receipt-backed result
  Capability --> Session: worker result
else direct plan insufficient
  Session -> ControllerBridge: optional planning request
  ControllerBridge --> Session: worker plan or clarification
end

Session --> UI: response
UI --> User: assistant output

note right of Substrate
This is the planned convergence seam
for workstation and governed runtime.
The runtime should consume this contract,
not the workstation package directly.
The same contract should expose
host-native and workstation-backed
implementations.
end note

@enduml
